  "result": "I found the cause and wrote a plan for a one-line fix. Nothing has been changed yet, and I haven't run anything to reproduce the problem. The order of the options themselves is fine. The problem is the order of the names within each option: help shows `--verbose, -v` and `--help, -h`, but the existing test at `tests/test_commands.py:188` expects `-h, --help`.\n\n**Cause:** `join_options` in `src/click/formatting.py:319` sorts an option's names with `reverse=True`. That puts the long `--` names before the short `-` names.\n\n**Planned fix:** remove `reverse=True` from that line:\n```python\nrv.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n```\nNames whose prefixes are the same length keep the order they were declared in. The fix also covers flag pairs like `--flag / --no-flag`.\n\n**To check it:** run `pytest tests/`, and run `--help` on a test command (via `CliRunner`) that has `-v/--verbose`. It should show `-v, --verbose` and `-h, --help`.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\the-help-output-looks-pure-gadget.md`. Let me know if you want me to go ahead.",
